 specialized knowledge within a particular interest. That's often something valuable and even celebrated. So, when the user's cousin observes this "nerdy" vibe, it's a valid observation for certain segments of the tech industry. But as they gain more experience, they'll likely see the full picture: developers are a far more diverse and multifaceted group than the stereotype would suggest.
